- Observe normal apply/capture, then emit a preparation marker at runtime.
- Concurrently write the suffix from another Redis connection.
- Kill/restart before confirmation: recover waiting barrier without crossing it.
- Drop an actual successful confirmation HTTP reply; explicitly retry/revalidate.
- Run successive Gateway adapter child processes with their own local files.
- Observe capture advancing while cold applied offset remains fixed.
- Kill/restart after confirmation: require online receipt revalidation.
- Reject old-boot and conflicting requests.
- Write 100 suffix values of 8192 bytes to cross the 4 MiB journal's 512 KiB
  conservative raw backlog threshold; observe stable paused capture/attempts.
- Verify cold suffix key absent and hot counter still 42.
- Gracefully stop while held, restart, recover held receipt and pressure pause.

